<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hugh O'Neill, Earl of Tyrone</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1550–<a href="/years/1616">1616</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hugh O'Neill, Earl of Tyrone, was the most powerful Gaelic lord of Ulster at the end of the 16th century. Raised partly under English influence, he led the Ulster lords, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-hugh-odonnell">Red Hugh O'Donnell</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-maguire-lord-of-fermanagh">Hugh Maguire</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a> and won at the Yellow Ford in 1598. Defeat at Kinsale in 1601 forced his submission, and in 1607 he left Ireland in the Flight of the Earls, dying in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hugh-oneill-earl-of-tyrone.jpg" alt="Hugh O'Neill, Earl of Tyrone" width="320" height="446" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hugh_O%27Neill,_1608.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
